00:19:05.677 --> 00:19:07.646 align:start size:50% position:50%
It's a new genre
of video game.

00:19:07.746 --> 00:19:10.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Dance video games or a music
  video come to life.
- Okay.

00:19:10.482 --> 00:19:14.386
Sherri:<i> Sega, they figured out
 what Nintendo forgot.</i>

00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:17.422
The whole point of home console
at the time

00:19:17.522 --> 00:19:21.894
was so that you can play
arcade games in your house.

00:19:21.994 --> 00:19:26.198 line:0%
<i> You got Street Fighter,
 Revenge of Shinobi,
 Double Dragon.</i>

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:27.933 line:0%
<i> You got Streets of Rage.</i>

00:19:28.033 --> 00:19:30.169 line:0%
Joe:<i> Now we had the violence
 that was isolated</i>

00:19:30.269 --> 00:19:32.738 line:0%
<i> to the arcade in the home.</i>

00:19:32.838 --> 00:19:35.774 line:0%
And that was a huge issue.

00:19:35.874 --> 00:19:37.576 line:0%
Hannibal:
<i> There's probably some stuff</i>

00:19:37.676 --> 00:19:40.412 line:0%
<i> we shouldn't have been exposed
 to at that age.</i>

00:19:40.512 --> 00:19:43.215 align:start size:91% position:9%
Ripping somebody's heart out,
even virtually

00:19:43.315 --> 00:19:45.951 line:0%
is probably somewhat damaging.

00:19:46.051 --> 00:19:47.819 line:0%
Blake:<i> In December of 1993,</i>

00:19:47.919 --> 00:19:50.622 line:0%
<i> Senator Joseph Lieberman
launched congressional hearings</i>

00:19:50.722 --> 00:19:52.558 line:0%
into video games and violence.

00:19:52.658 --> 00:19:54.626 line:0%
Lieberman:<i> In the first segment,
 which is Sega's version,</i>

00:19:54.726 --> 00:19:56.862 line:0%
<i> the player may then choose
 a method of murder</i>

00:19:56.962 --> 00:19:59.831 line:0%
<i> ranging from ripping
 a heart out</i>

00:19:59.931 --> 00:20:02.301 line:0%
to pulling off the head
of the opponent

00:20:02.401 --> 00:20:03.902 line:0%
with spinal cord attached.

00:20:04.002 --> 00:20:07.806 line:0%
Sherri:<i> What happens
 after the hearing is the start</i>

00:20:07.906 --> 00:20:10.275 line:0%
<i> of the entertainment software
 ratings board.</i>

00:20:10.375 --> 00:20:11.777 line:0%
The ESRB.

00:20:11.877 --> 00:20:15.214 line:0%
Joe:<i> The little E, the T,
 the M, and the A</i>

00:20:15.314 --> 00:20:17.783 line:0%
<i> that's in the bottom corner
 of every video game,</i>

00:20:17.883 --> 00:20:19.718 line:0%
<i> that is because
 of Sega Genesis.</i>

00:20:19.818 --> 00:20:21.787 line:0%
That was when Sega finally
started passing Nintendo.

00:20:21.887 --> 00:20:23.956 line:0%
Marques:<i> Sega successfully
 positioned themselves</i>

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:26.525 line:0%
<i> as the sophisticated
 alternative to Nintendo.</i>

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.897
<i> But holding onto that lead
 proved to be a bigger
 challenge.</i>

00:20:34.799 --> 00:20:36.568
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:20:36.668 --> 00:20:38.770
Adesina:<i> So, even though
 the Genesis was crushing it,</i>

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:41.740
<i> the video game industry is
 constantly changing
 and evolving</i>

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.009 line:0%
<i> and everyone has to keep up.</i>

00:20:44.109 --> 00:20:47.379 line:0%
Sherri:<i> So in 1999, Sega wants
 to step it up a notch</i>

00:20:47.479 --> 00:20:50.882 line:0%
<i>and they release the Dreamcast.</i>

00:20:50.982 --> 00:20:53.685
But a new challenger had entered
the arena.

00:20:53.785 --> 00:20:58.357
<i> Sony is now in the game
 with the PlayStation.</i>

00:20:58.457 --> 00:21:01.793
<i> Unfortunately, the Dreamcast
 was not well-received</i>

00:21:01.893 --> 00:21:04.596
and they pulled out
of the console wars.
They lost.

00:21:04.696 --> 00:21:07.499 line:0%
Adesina:<i> And in 2001,
 Sega finally bowed out</i>

00:21:07.599 --> 00:21:09.534 line:0%
and stopped making consoles.

00:21:16.541 --> 00:21:18.477
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:21:20.912 --> 00:21:24.916
What would you say is the legacy
of Sega Genesis?

00:21:25.016 --> 00:21:27.052
Blake:
<i> Why does Sega Genesis matter?</i>

00:21:27.152 --> 00:21:28.754
It's because we would not have

00:21:28.854 --> 00:21:31.523
the modern-day video
game industry.

00:21:31.623 --> 00:21:33.525
<i> They expanded
 the demographic of gaming</i>

00:21:33.625 --> 00:21:37.396
<i> and showed that there was room
 for more than one console.</i>

00:21:37.496 --> 00:21:40.399
Hannibal:<i> The Genesis was a big
 part of my childhood.</i>

00:21:40.499 --> 00:21:41.933
<i>Spent a lot of time on it, man.</i>

00:21:42.033 --> 00:21:44.703
It was-- It was dope.

00:21:44.803 --> 00:21:46.938
Sherri:<i> It's the first console</i>

00:21:47.038 --> 00:21:50.776
<i> that ever threatened
 Nintendo's kingdom.</i>

00:21:50.876 --> 00:21:54.479
Without Sega constantly
innovating,

00:21:54.579 --> 00:21:56.081 line:0%
<i> Nintendo probably would've sat</i>

00:21:56.181 --> 00:22:00.052 line:0%
<i>on its laurels for a long time.</i>

00:22:00.152 --> 00:22:03.789 line:0%
<i> I don't think we would've
 gotten to 64-bit
 Gravis consoles</i>

00:22:03.889 --> 00:22:06.091 line:0%
<i> in a reasonable time.</i>

00:22:06.191 --> 00:22:08.460 line:0%
<i> Sega made Nintendo better</i>

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:12.564 line:0%
because competition breeds
innovation.

00:22:12.664 --> 00:22:13.999
Adesina: 
<i> The Genesis showed me</i>

00:22:14.099 --> 00:22:16.401 line:0%
<i> where technology
 and art come together</i>

00:22:16.501 --> 00:22:19.504 line:0%
<i> because it was just so
 beautiful in terms of
 its graphic output.</i>

00:22:19.604 --> 00:22:21.840
<i> It's actually what inspired me</i>

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.343
<i> to wanna become a video game
 developer.</i>

00:22:24.443 --> 00:22:29.348
Sega really changed the course
of my career and my life.

00:22:29.448 --> 00:22:31.950
Joe:<i> Sega influenced
 how we play games</i>

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.985
<i> because if it was
 just the Nintendo</i>

00:22:34.085 --> 00:22:36.621
<i> maybe we wouldn't have
 the cool,</i>

00:22:36.721 --> 00:22:38.457
aggressive games
that we have now.

00:22:38.557 --> 00:22:40.792 line:0%
<i> Assassin's Creed,
 the Call of Duties.</i>

00:22:40.892 --> 00:22:45.063 line:0%
Those games found their
beginning with the Sega Genesis.

00:22:45.163 --> 00:22:48.600
Blake:<i> The battle between Sega
 and Nintendo pushed each other
 to the limits.</i>

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:51.503
I think the victor is obvious.
It's us.

00:22:51.603 --> 00:22:53.405 align:start size:59% position:41%
It's the gamers.
It's the consumers.

00:22:53.505 --> 00:22:55.407
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:22:55.507 --> 00:22:57.409
<i> Without Sega I'm not sure</i>

00:22:57.509 --> 00:22:59.010
<i> where the state
 of video games would be,</i>

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:01.780
but I believe
that we're all better for it.

00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:04.950
<i> And that's what will always
 make the Genesis the most
 important console,</i>

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:08.653
<i> in my opinion.</i>

00:23:08.753 --> 00:23:11.857
Marques:<i> I really think
 if I was a gamer in the '90s,</i>

00:23:11.957 --> 00:23:15.127
<i> I'd probably would've been
 a Sega Genesis gamer.</i>

00:23:15.227 --> 00:23:16.695
Not just because
it was matte black.

00:23:16.795 --> 00:23:18.964
Although, that is pretty sweet.

00:23:19.064 --> 00:23:20.966 line:0%
<i> But because its place
 in history</i>

00:23:21.066 --> 00:23:25.137 line:0%
<i>as this first big competitor to
a goliath really speaks to me.</i>

00:23:25.237 --> 00:23:27.906 line:0%
<i> Competition breeds innovation.</i>

00:23:28.006 --> 00:23:29.841 line:0%
It's true.

00:23:29.941 --> 00:23:33.845 line:0%
And that's my favorite part of
the legacy of the Sega Genesis.

00:23:33.945 --> 00:23:35.847 line:0%
Thanks for watching.

00:23:35.947 --> 00:23:37.516 line:0%
Catch you guys on the next one.
Peace.

